# Build context for src/Library.Api/Dockerfile, which builds from the repository
# root because the projects reference each other across directories.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` after restoring. Without this file that copy
# drags in whatever the host happens to have lying around -- build output
# compiled for another OS, with absolute paths from another machine -- and lays
# it on top of what the image just restored for itself. `dotnet publish
# --no-restore` then reads a project.assets.json written by someone else's
# NuGet and fails. Everything below is either reproduced inside the image or
# has no business being in it.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/

# The web image builds from ./web with its own context; the API does not need it.
web/

.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local configuration and anything holding a secret.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/*.user

# Not part of the product.
inputs/
scripts/
README.md
docker-compose.yml
**/*.md
